olicy","content":"`dev-build.yml`"},"369":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-48","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#tag-policy","content":"Rolling rebuild on every push to `dev`; `linux/amd64` only."},"370":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-49","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#tag-policy","content":"`dev-<sha>`"},"371":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-50","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#tag-policy","content":"`dev-build.yml`"},"372":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-51","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#tag-policy","content":"Immutable snapshot of the same build, for pinning and rollback."},"373":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-52","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#tag-policy","content":"Treat `dev` images as integration builds, not production deployments."},"374":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-53","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#ports","content":"Port"},"375":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-54","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#ports","content":"Purpose"},"376":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-55","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#ports","content":"`5900`"},"377":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-56","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#ports","content":"VNC (remote desktop — needed to scan-login QQ)"},"378":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-57","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#ports","content":"`6081`"},"379":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-58","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#ports","content":"noVNC (browser VNC, no client needed)"},"380":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-59","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#ports","content":"`5099`"},"381":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-60","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#ports","content":"SnowLuma WebUI"},"382":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-61","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#ports","content":"`3000`"},"383":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-62","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#ports","content":"OneBot HTTP (default)"},"384":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-63","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#ports","content":"`3001`"},"385":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-64","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#ports","content":"OneBot WebSocket (default)"},"386":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-65","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#host-setup-relax-the-ptrace-policy","content":"**Do this before starting the container, otherwise hook injection will fail at runtime.**"},"387":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-66","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#host-setup-relax-the-ptrace-policy","content":"SnowLuma's native addon uses `ptrace` to inject the hook into the in-container QQ process. Modern Linux distros (Ubuntu / Debian / Arch / …) ship with `kernel.yama.ptrace_scope` set to `1` or higher, which means **even with `--cap-add=SYS_PTRACE` on the container, the host kernel still blocks the ptrace call**."},"388":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-67","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#host-setup-relax-the-ptrace-policy","content":"Run **once** on the host:"},"389":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-68","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#host-setup-relax-the-ptrace-policy","content":"Verify:"},"390":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-69","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#host-setup-relax-the-ptrace-policy","content":"Writing to `/etc/sysctl.d/99-snowluma-ptrace.conf` keeps the setting across reboots. If your host has stricter security requirements (multi-tenant, internet-facing), prefer a dedicated isolated host (bare metal / VM) over relaxing the system-wide policy."},"391":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-70","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#one-line-docker-run","content":"`--cap-add=SYS_PTRACE` and `--security-opt seccomp=unconfined` are **mandatory**. SnowLuma's native addon uses ptrace to inject the hook into the QQ process; the default seccomp profile blocks that."},"392":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-71","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#one-line-docker-run","content":"`--shm-size=1g` is needed for QQ's Chromium runtime — the default container `/dev/shm` is too small and QQ will crash."},"393":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-72","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#docker-compose","content":"Recommended over `docker run`. The main repo already ships `docker/docker-compose.yml` — use it as-is."},"394":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-73","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#docker-compose","content":"`ulimits.nofile` exists for multi-account setups: one account is fine, but each QQ is a full Chromium process and three or four of them will hit the default 1024 descriptor limit — you'll see `EMFILE: too many open files` in the logs."},"395":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-74","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#docker-compose","content":"noVNC / WebUI / VNC bind `127.0.0.1` by default, so nothing is reachable from the public interface. Two ways to get in:"},"396":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-75","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#docker-compose","content":"Start (from the repo root):"},"397":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-76","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#docker-compose","content":"Upgrade:"},"398":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-77","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#docker-compose","content":"To track one specific version, pin it in `.env`:"},"399":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-78","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"Var"},"400":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-79","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"Default"},"401":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-80","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"Notes"},"402":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-81","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`VNC_PASSWD`"},"403":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-82","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`vncpasswd`"},"404":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-83","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"VNC / noVNC login password. **Change this**, otherwise anyone can see your QQ desktop."},"405":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-84","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_UID`"},"406":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-85","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`1000`"},"407":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-86","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"uid of the in-container `snowluma` user. Match it to the host owner of your mounted volumes."},"408":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-87","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_GID`"},"409":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-88","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`1000`"},"410":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-89","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"gid of the in-container `snowluma` user."},"411":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-90","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_WEBUI_HOST`"},"412":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-91","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`0.0.0.0`"},"413":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-92","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"WebUI bind address. The binary itself binds loopback only; the image opens it up, otherwise the published port can't reach it."},"414":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-93","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_WEBUI_PORT`"},"415":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-94","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`5099`"},"416":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-95","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"WebUI listen port (inside the container)."},"417":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-96","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_LOG_LEVEL`"},"418":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-97","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`info`"},"419":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-98","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`error` / `warn` / `info` / `debug`."},"420":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-99","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_SCREEN`"},"421":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-100","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`1920x1080x24`"},"422":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-101","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"Xvfb resolution + color depth."},"423":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-102","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_HOOK_AUTOLOAD`"},"424":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-103","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`1`"},"425":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-104","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"Image opts into auto-injection by default. Set `0` to fall back to the manual Load workflow."},"426":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-105","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_QQ_FLAGS`"},"427":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-106","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"empty"},"428":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-107","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"Extra flags appended to the QQ command line, space separated. On GPU-less hosts try `--disable-gpu --disable-software-rasterizer`."},"429":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-108","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"`SNOWLUMA_EXTRA_QQ_HOMES`"},"430":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-109","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"empty"},"431":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-110","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"Extra QQ account `HOME` directories, comma or space separated; each one gets its own supervisord program. See multiple accounts."},"432":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-111","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#environment-variables","content":"Environment variables override `runtime.json`, so they're the ergonomic knob in Docker."},"433":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-112","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#volumes","content":"Volume"},"434":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-113","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#volumes","content":"Container path"},"435":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-114","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#volumes","content":"Contents"},"436":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-115","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#volumes","content":"`snowluma-data`"},"437":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-116","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#volumes","content":"`/app/snowluma-data`"},"438":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-117","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#volumes","content":"SnowLuma config, cache, SQLite. Includes `config/onebot.json` and `config/runtime.json`."},"439":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-118","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#volumes","content":"`snowluma-qq-config`"},"440":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-119","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#volumes","content":"`/app/.config`"},"441":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-120","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#volumes","content":"QQ client config."},"442":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-121","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#volumes","content":"`snowluma-qq-data`"},"443":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-122","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#volumes","content":"`/app/.local/share`"},"444":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-123","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#volumes","content":"QQ user data (login state, cache)."},"445":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-124","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#volumes","content":"**Don't delete these on upgrade** — you'll lose login state and configuration."},"446":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-125","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#first-time-login","content":"Open `http://<host>:6081/` (noVNC) and enter `VNC_PASSWD`."},"447":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-126","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#first-time-login","content":"Inside the remote desktop you'll see QQ already running. Scan the QR to log in."},"448":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-127","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#first-time-login","content":"Once login completes the hook auto-switches from passive observation to working mode — no need to click Load in the WebUI."},"449":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-128","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#first-time-login","content":"Open `http://<host>:5099/` for the SnowLuma WebUI."},"450":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-129","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#finding-the-webui-bootstrap-password","content":"On a fresh data volume the first launch logs a one-time password:"},"451":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-130","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#finding-the-webui-bootstrap-password","content":"Just the password string:"},"452":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-131","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#finding-the-webui-bootstrap-password","content":"The bootstrap password is logged **only on a brand-new data volume's first boot**. Reusing the volume or restarting won't regenerate it."},"453":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-132","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#running-multiple-qq-accounts","content":"Linux QQ ships a single-instance lock — clicking the QQ icon again on a desktop that already has one running just focuses the existing window, it doesn't start a second process. The lock file lives at `$HOME/.config/QQ/SingletonLock`, so every instance needs its &#x2A;*own `HOME`**."},"454":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-133","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#running-multiple-qq-accounts","content":"SnowLuma needs no extra configuration: HookManager walks every QQ main process it can find, injects the hook into each, and spins up a separate `OneBotInstance` per UIN with its own `config/onebot_<uin>.json`."},"455":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-134","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#declare-them-with-snowluma_extra_qq_homes-recommended","content":"List the extra `HOME` directories and supervisord manages one QQ process per entry — a crash restarts **only that account**, leaving the others untouched:"},"456":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-135","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#declare-them-with-snowluma_extra_qq_homes-recommended","content":"Separate paths with commas or spaces. The leading `/app` (primary account) is skipped automatically; duplicates and relative paths are ignored with a message in the log. Missing directories are created at startup."},"457":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-136","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#declare-them-with-snowluma_extra_qq_homes-recommended","content":"After boot, `docker logs snowluma` prints something like:"},"458":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-137","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#declare-them-with-snowluma_extra_qq_homes-recommended","content":"Each account becomes a `[program:qq-<dirname>]` you can inspect individually:"},"459":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-138","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#declare-them-with-snowluma_extra_qq_homes-recommended","content":"**Don't forget the volumes.** Declaring a HOME without mounting a volume for it means the account logs in fine but loses its session when the container is recreated."},"460":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-139","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#starting-one-by-hand-from-the-novnc-desktop","content":"For a throwaway account you don't want in compose, use the noVNC terminal:"},"461":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-140","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#starting-one-by-hand-from-the-novnc-desktop","content":"`disown` detaches QQ from the terminal so closing the window won't kill it. This path does not restart automatically and does not survive a container restart."},"462":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-141","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#caveats","content":"**One HOME per QQ instance** — never share a `HOME` between two QQs; they'll fight over the lock file."},"463":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-142","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#caveats","content":"**Resources**: each QQ is a full Chromium process, \\~300-500 MB RAM. The default `--shm-size=1g` is fine for one; bump to `2gb`+ for multi-account."},"464":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-143","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#caveats","content":"**All windows share the same Xvfb desktop**: noVNC shows every QQ window; minimize the ones you've already logged into. Hook keeps working regardless of window state."},"465":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-144","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/docker#caveats","content":"**WebUI lists every UIN automatically**: no manual configuration — SnowLuma surfaces each new account in the WebUI and `get_login_info` returns the new UINs once login completes."},"466":{"id":"/en/docs/docker-145","page_id":"/en/docs/docker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/d